-- An L4 name that lands exactly on a name the generated runtime module exports.
--
-- `--package` writes `modules: [.l4runtime]`, which docassemble execs as
-- `from <pkg>.l4runtime import *` (parse.py:8572 at 1b6678384) into the
-- interview dict on EVERY assemble pass. The runtime module's `__all__` bounds
-- which names arrive; it does nothing to stop an interview variable from being
-- one of them, and the loser is the interview's. Unreserved, this export's goal
-- variable `l4_source_text` was clobbered by the imported function object --
-- truthy -- so the PACKAGED artifact asked no question at all and returned the
-- opposite verdict to the bare one, with the fidelity report saying
-- "(nothing lost)". That breaks R11 decision 6: the two artifact shapes must
-- mean the same thing.
--
-- Expect the goal variable to be `l4_source_text_`, in BOTH artifact shapes:
-- the shapes must not disagree about a variable's name either.

DECLARE Filing
    HAS
      @desc whether the filing arrived before the deadline
      `filed on time` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Whether the filing is good
GIVEN d IS A Filing @desc The filing under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `L4 source text` d IF d's `filed on time`

#EVAL `L4 source text` OF Filing WITH `filed on time` IS FALSE
-- FALSE
